MarketLens is an interactive prediction market analytics dashboard built around live Kalshi data.
It helps users explore market implied probabilities, recent price movement, trading volume, historical trends,
and order book activity through an interactive visual interface.

The main dashboard gives an overview of active prediction markets and includes an interactive Market Map where:

- the x-axis represents current market-implied probability
- the y-axis represents 24-hour probability change
- bubble size represents trading volume

Users can hover over markets for more information, click into individual markets, view historical probability charts, inspect volume and open interest, and explore the current order book.

Each market also includes an optional AI Market Brief that summarizes the calculated market data in plain language.


How to use:
1. Open the MarketLens website.
2. Explore the Market Map and hover over bubbles for market details.
3. Click a market to open its full detail page.
4. View its historical probability chart, volume, open interest, order book, and resolution information.
5. Click Generate Market Brief to receive a short AI generated explanation of the market's current pricing and recent movement.

Features I Am Most Proud Of
The Market Map is the main visualization in the project. It lets users compare many markets at once
using probability, 24-hour movement, and trading volume.

Live Kalshi Data
The application uses real prediction market data from Kalshi through a Flask backend rather than relying only on static sample data.

Historical Market Exploration
Individual market pages include real historical probability data and interactive charts so users can explore how market pricing changes over time.

AI Market Brief
The AI feature is intentionally separated from the analysis. Python calculates the probability changes, volatility, volume information, and other statistics first. Gemini only receives those values and explains them in language.
